  "page_text": "~rabbits/uxn5 - Varvara Ordinator, written in Javascript(HTML5) - sourcehut git sourcehut Log in — Register ~rabbits/uxn project sources mailing lists tickets uxn5 summary tree log refs Varvara Ordinator, written in Javascript(HTML5) 4da440f0 — Devine Lu Linvega 5 months ago Fixed drawing distance 9cbca360 — Devine Lu Linvega 5 months ago Screen/pixel make use of flipxy c2eaf8d9 — Devine Lu Linvega 6 months ago Removed boot rom refs main browse log 80K release notes clone read-only https://git.sr.ht/~rabbits/uxn5 read/write git@git.sr.ht:~rabbits/uxn5 Clone repo to your account You can also use your local clone with git send-email. .highlight { background: inherit; }#Uxn5 An emulator for the Uxn stack-machine, written in Javascript. Check out a live demo at rabbits.srht.site/uxn5 #Usage Include the uxn core in your <head> tag: <script src=\"src/uxn.js\"></script> Include the boot sequence in your website, and evaluate a program: <script type=\"text/javascript\"> const uxn = new Uxn() uxn.load(program).eval(0x0100) </script> #Including Rom If you would like to include a rom directly in the emulator, modify boot.js and add the rom as compressed base64 ulz encoded string, like: const boot_ulz = \"ASYUyuASyu_7ASHhua...\"; #Need a hand? The following resources are a good place to start: XXIIVV — uxntal XXIIVV — uxntal reference compudanzas — uxn tutorial You can also find us in #uxn on irc.esper.net. #Contributing Submit patches using git send-email to the ~rabbits/public-inbox mailing list. Repository RID: 06dy9xvcssw2v2w971perjv5n0",
